  1.GPU (Graphics Card): I would upgrade the GPU first because it handles graphics, textures, lighting, and frame rates.
A better graphics card would provide smoother gameplay and higher visual quality.

2. RAM: I would upgrade to at least 16 GB of RAM if the PC has less.
More RAM helps the game and other background applications run smoothly without slowing down the system.

3.SSD: If the PC still uses an HDD, I would upgrade to an SSD.
An SSD would make the game load faster and improve overall system responsiveness.

4.CPU (Processor): A faster CPU would help the game process player movements, 
AI, physics, and other game calculations more efficiently, reducing lag and stuttering.

5.Cooling System: A better CPU cooler or additional case fans may be needed to prevent
overheating during long gaming sessions and maintain consistent performance.
